# __name__

A minimal Go CLI generated by `weld`. The base project is deliberately small:
a command dispatcher, a structured logger and nothing else. It has no HTTP
server, no database and no frontend — those arrive later as capabilities.

## Commands

```sh
go run . version   # print the version
go run . help      # list the available commands
```

```sh
make build   # build bin/__name__
make run     # run the app (pass a subcommand with ARGS, e.g. make run ARGS=serve)
make test    # run the Go tests
```

## Extending the project

The project is scaffolded from the `base` capability (v__version__). Every file
weld wrote is recorded in `weld.json` with the capability and version that
produced it.

Capabilities are additive and dependency-resolved: each adds its own files and
registers its own commands, and `weld add` installs any missing dependency
first.

```sh
weld add web   # installs the http capability, then the React + TS + Vite frontend
weld add api   # installs the http capability, then the JSON API + OpenAPI 3.1
weld add db    # PostgreSQL: SQL migrations, sqlc queries and a repository (no HTTP)
```

`weld add web` installs `http`, which owns the `serve` command and the HTTP
server, and then the frontend it serves. `weld add api` installs the same
`http` capability and adds the JSON API under `/api/`; it does not require the
frontend. `web` and `api` are independent, so they can be added in either order
and both are served by the one `serve` command. `weld add db` requires only this
base project: it adds PostgreSQL persistence without an HTTP server, so it works
in a CLI-only project and composes with `http`/`web`/`api` in any order.

The frontend reserves `/api/` for the API capability: unknown API paths return a
not-found rather than the HTML shell. The base project does not install or
require any capability.

Use `weld list` to see what is available and installed.

## Command extension point

`internal/app` exposes `RegisterCommand`, the one Go extension point capabilities
use. A capability adds a file whose `init` registers its command:

```go
func init() {
	app.RegisterCommand(app.Command{Name: "serve", Summary: "...", Run: runServe})
}
```

With no capability installed the CLI still builds and runs with `version` and
`help` alone.

## Layout

```
main.go            command entry point; builds the logger and logs a failed command
internal/app/      command dispatch and the capability command registry
internal/logging/  log/slog factory: New(w io.Writer, format, options)
Makefile           build/run/test entry points
weld.json          manifest of capability-managed files
```
